{"id": "EUVD-2026-59668", "enisaUuid": "72d23a01-2e6a-3500-af65-ac47e8339fa4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvxlan: use neigh_ha_snapshot() in route_shortcircuit()\n\nThe neighbour hardware address n->ha can be updated asynchronously by the\nneighbour subsystem, protected by n->ha_lock seqlock. Reading n->ha without\nholding the seqlock loop can lead to torn reads or reading a partially updated\nMAC address.\n\nUse neigh_ha_snapshot() in route_shortcircuit() to safely copy n->ha under\nread_seqbegin()/read_seqretry() lock protection before using it.\n\nNote that arp_reduce() and neigh_reduce() seem to have the same issue\nleft for future patches.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T12:27:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:05:48", "baseScore": 10.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:L", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/32a9590a8d30426e3db63e6b20893e47e02576c0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d0993fc053f29e15cc7c9fe2029df3882a2ab5ab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/87210054bad82bbae6f483a742dc45722fb47a6b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d08e8ac13f2e228cc7fc3c70b5ebe71557b624a0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ec341bb76d77b4c2948764375ee6bfeef4bb41c3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff89415d34c3ab9f5312316423122e664ed3524f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/05f2987f73daa05333fd713d05546142f9f7c5f0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8eca411347e1d38964f9ed2c8d3b6ab0e7e4473d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-g8xx-g6f9-m789", "CVE-2026-74475"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e11604b-1a00-3f77-97b5-f70c892dff10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.8"}, {"id": "0f7f5eb6-8742-3b6c-a17d-d96735cad2ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.103"}, {"id": "10e24a66-5740-396a-8f3b-68d5edd2b1c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor":